From 9e50aaec2a87f50b6252e4b902a52c8a710d7f11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:26:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] wayland: report the compositor's window buttons in
 enabled_buttons

xdg-shell v5 lets a compositor say which of its window operations it
offers a toplevel (wm_capabilities: window menu, maximize, fullscreen,
minimize). sctk decodes them into each configure, and winit's own
fallback frame draws only the buttons they allow, but
Window::enabled_buttons always returned WindowButtons::all(), so an
application drawing its own decorations had no way to leave out a
minimize button on a compositor that cannot minimize (sway), or a
maximize button on one that cannot maximize.

enabled_buttons now returns CLOSE, and MINIMIZE and MAXIMIZE where the
last configure's capabilities include them. A compositor that sends no
wm_capabilities offers everything, as the protocol says and as sctk
assumes, and so does a window not configured yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

